   320	 * Resolve identity keys to their owning entity — TYPE-AGNOSTIC.
   321	 *
   322	 * An identity value belongs to at most ONE entity org-wide (the
   323	 * `idx_entity_identities_live_unique` index on `(org, namespace, identifier)`),
   324	 * so a key resolves to a single entity of ANY type. We deliberately do NOT
   325	 * filter by the rule's target `entityType`: a `slack_user_id` owned by a
   326	 * signed-in `$member` must resolve to that `$member` even when a `person`-typed
   327	 * rule looks it up, so attribution and ACL converge on one entity instead of
   328	 * minting a duplicate `person` (the #1646 cross-source collapse, now automatic).
