   205	    // ENTITY but leaves its `entity_identities` rows live, still pointing at
   206	    // it (only a merge or sign-in adoption repoints them). Matching on the
   207	    // identity alone therefore resolves onto a dead entity, writes `member_of`
   208	    // to it, and never mints a replacement — so the member silently vanishes
